{
  "root_node": "model.dim_customers",
  "cause": "code_change",
  "action": "patch",
  "evidence": "stg_customers has 1500 rows with 1500 distinct customer_key (no duplicates). dim_customers has 7500 rows but only 1500 distinct customer_key, indicating each key appears 5 times. The dim_customers SQL joins stg_customers to stg_nations correctly, but the second join uses `on n.region_key = n.region_key`, which is always true, causing a cross join with all 5 rows of stg_regions. This multiplies each customer row by 5, creating duplicate customer_key rows. Fix by changing the join condition to `on r.region_key = n.region_key`."
}
